1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,232
Buyers ask to send items back from their order, and you decide.

2
00:00:05,232 --> 00:00:09,402
This video shows how to set up returns, what a buyer does, and

3
00:00:09,402 --> 00:00:13,020
how to approve, receive, refund or exchange a return.

4
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:23,037
A shopper who is not sure they can send something back is a shopper who hesitates.

5
00:00:23,037 --> 00:00:25,130
A clear return policy sells.

6
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:30,773
Handled by email, returns lose track of what was asked, what was agreed,

7
00:00:30,773 --> 00:00:32,530
and what was refunded.

8
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:37,999
Returns lets buyers ask to send items back from their own order page.

9
00:00:37,999 --> 00:00:43,032
You approve or decline, mark the items received, put them back into stock,

10
00:00:43,032 --> 00:00:44,920
then refund or exchange.

11
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:49,650
Each step is emailed to the buyer and written in the order's notes.

12
00:00:53,850 --> 00:00:57,878
You set a return window, the reasons a buyer can choose from, whether

13
00:00:57,878 --> 00:01:01,530
exchanges are offered, and what to tell them once you approve.

14
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:05,819
A buyer asks from a paid order, for their money back or for

15
00:01:05,819 --> 00:01:08,160
something else, such as another size.

16
00:01:08,910 --> 00:01:14,930
You approve or decline, mark the items received, and choose what goes back into stock.

17
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:20,805
Then you refund the buyer, or send the replacement and close the return.

18
00:01:20,805 --> 00:01:22,710
Open Commerce, Returns.

19
00:01:26,919 --> 00:01:29,524
Open Settings, Commerce, Returns.

20
00:01:29,524 --> 00:01:35,270
The Return window is how many days after paying a buyer can ask to return items.

21
00:01:35,270 --> 00:01:36,739
It starts at 30.

22
00:01:37,193 --> 00:01:42,031
Reasons, one for each line, are what buyers choose from for each item.

23
00:01:42,031 --> 00:01:46,933
Let buyers ask for something else instead of a refund offers exchanges.

24
00:01:47,412 --> 00:01:51,716
Return instructions are what the buyer is told once you approve a return,

25
00:01:51,716 --> 00:01:53,786
such as where to send the items.

26
00:01:53,786 --> 00:01:54,712
Click Save.

27
00:01:58,919 --> 00:02:02,910
A paid order with goods shows a Returns box on its page, in

28
00:02:02,910 --> 00:02:06,532
the buyer's account or on the order link a guest has.

29
00:02:06,532 --> 00:02:09,909
While the window is open, it offers Return items.

30
00:02:10,447 --> 00:02:13,579
The buyer chooses How many of each item, and Why.

31
00:02:13,579 --> 00:02:17,964
Downloads and services have nothing to send back, and an item cannot be

32
00:02:17,964 --> 00:02:20,527
returned more times than it was bought.

33
00:02:20,977 --> 00:02:25,564
They choose My money back, or with exchanges on, Something else instead, and

34
00:02:25,564 --> 00:02:27,297
say what they would like.

35
00:02:27,297 --> 00:02:30,317
They can add a comment, and click Ask to return.

36
00:02:30,772 --> 00:02:35,164
The request is emailed, and the Returns box lists it as Requested, with

37
00:02:35,164 --> 00:02:37,732
Withdraw this request until you answer.

38
00:02:41,938 --> 00:02:45,768
Commerce, Returns lists the returns, newest first.

39
00:02:45,768 --> 00:02:49,872
Search by return or order number, or filter by status.

40
00:02:49,872 --> 00:02:54,318
Open one to see what is coming back, why, what it was paid,

41
00:02:54,318 --> 00:02:56,438
and what the buyer wrote.

42
00:02:56,890 --> 00:03:01,214
Under Approve, add a message for the buyer if you like, and click Approve.

43
00:03:01,214 --> 00:03:05,862
They are emailed your return instructions, your message and the return number to

44
00:03:05,862 --> 00:03:07,160
put in the parcel.

45
00:03:07,688 --> 00:03:12,495
When the items arrive, tick what can be sold again, and click Mark received.

46
00:03:12,495 --> 00:03:14,958
The ticked items go back into stock.

47
00:03:15,424 --> 00:03:19,593
For a buyer who wants their money back, Refund starts at what the

48
00:03:19,593 --> 00:03:22,352
items were paid, before tax and shipping.

49
00:03:22,352 --> 00:03:26,874
Click Refund and close, and the money goes back the way the buyer paid.

50
00:03:31,106 --> 00:03:35,751
For a buyer who wants something else, the page shows what they asked for.

51
00:03:35,751 --> 00:03:38,808
Under Decline, say why, and the buyer is told.

52
00:03:38,808 --> 00:03:41,806
You can decline until the items are received.

53
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:44,662
To agree, approve the return first.

54
00:03:44,662 --> 00:03:46,772
The Exchange box then appears.

55
00:03:46,772 --> 00:03:50,992
Send them what they asked for, add a message, such as the tracking

56
00:03:50,992 --> 00:03:54,156
number, and click The replacement is on its way.

57
00:03:54,156 --> 00:03:57,380
The return is completed and the buyer is emailed.

58
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:04,680
The return window runs from when the order was paid.

59
00:04:05,430 --> 00:04:07,412
Returns start with the buyer.

60
00:04:07,412 --> 00:04:10,810
Refunding an order outright stays on the order's page.

61
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:15,368
Items you mark as sellable go back into stock, in the location you

62
00:04:15,368 --> 00:04:18,330
choose when you keep stock in more than one place.

63
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:22,316
Emails need your site's email to be set up.

64
00:04:22,316 --> 00:04:26,280
Without it, returns still work, and nobody is emailed.

65
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:31,483
Clothing:

66
00:04:31,483 --> 00:04:34,560
let buyers swap a size without a refund.

67
00:04:35,310 --> 00:04:36,952
Damaged on arrival:

68
00:04:36,952 --> 00:04:39,580
refund before the item comes back.

69
00:04:40,330 --> 00:04:41,618
Out of window:

70
00:04:41,618 --> 00:04:43,810
decline with a clear reason.

71
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:46,871
A longer window for the holidays:

72
00:04:46,871 --> 00:04:49,480
change the return window for a season.

73
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:57,203
Set the window, let buyers ask, and approve, receive and close each return.

74
00:04:57,203 --> 00:04:59,040
Thanks for watching.

